==Election results==
===2026 election===
The [[2026 New Zealand general election|next election]] will be held on 7 November 2026. Candidates for Kaipara ki Mahurangi are listed at ''[[Candidates in the 2026 New Zealand general election by electorate#Kaipara ki Mahurangi|Candidates in the 2026 New Zealand general election by electorate § Kaipara ki Mahurangi]]''. Official results will be available after 27 November 2026.<ref name="ge2026_dates">{{Cite web |last= |date=2026 |title=Key dates |url=https://vote.nz/2026-general-election/about/overview/key-dates |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260415030403/https://vote.nz/2026-general-election/about/overview/key-dates |archive-date=15 April 2026 |access-date=27 April 2026 |website=Vote NZ}}</ref> Due to [[Chris Penk|Chris Penk's]] failed National Party leadership coup against [[Christopher Luxon]], Penk will not seek re-election in the 2026 election.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Aotearoa |first=RNZ {{!}} Te Reo Irirangi o |date=12 August 2026 |title=Chris Penk says he will not seek re-election after losing ministerial portfolios |url=https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics/975747/chris-penk-says-he-will-not-seek-re-election-after-losing-ministerial-portfolios |access-date=16 August 2026 |website=RNZ |language=en-nz}}</ref>

